.TH SDL_HINT_MOUSE_DPI_SCALE_CURSORS 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MOUSE_DPI_SCALE_CURSORS \- A variable setting whether we should scale cursors by the current display scale.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MOUSE_DPI_SCALE_CURSORS \(dqSDL_MOUSE_DPI_SCALE_CURSORS\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Cursors will not change size based on the display content scale\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Cursors will automatically match the display content scale (e\[char46]g\[char46] a 2x sized cursor will be used when the window is on a monitor with 200% scale)\[char46] This is currently implemented on Windows\[char46]
.PP
This hint needs to be set before creating cursors\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

